* Real-Time Neural Video Compression & Streaming Engine <<root>>

** 1. Foundations & Problem Definition <<phase>>
*** 1.1 Literature Review & Problem Identification
**** 1.1.1 Conventional Codec Review (H.264 / H.265 / AV1)
**** 1.1.2 VAE & Learned Compression Literature (Kingma & Welling, Balle et al.)
**** 1.1.3 Problem Statement & Project Scope Freeze
**** 1.1.4 Synopsis & PERT Chart Submission
*** 1.2 Dataset Collection & Preprocessing
**** 1.2.1 Dataset Selection & Acquisition (DAVIS, Vimeo-90K, UVG-HD)
**** 1.2.2 Frame Extraction Pipeline (Video & Image-Sequence Sources)
**** 1.2.3 Resize, Normalize & Augmentation Transforms
**** 1.2.4 Leak-Free Train / Val / Test Split & Manifest Generation

** 2. System & Data Architecture Design <<phase>>
*** 2.1 Encoder / Decoder Architecture Design
**** 2.1.1 Convolutional Downsampling Stack
**** 2.1.2 Mirrored Transposed-Convolution Decoder
**** 2.1.3 Latent Dimension & Channel Sizing
*** 2.2 PyTorch Data Pipeline Design
**** 2.2.1 FrameDataset Specification
**** 2.2.2 Train / Eval Transform Pipelines
**** 2.2.3 DataLoader Factories
*** 2.3 Feasibility & Project Planning
**** 2.3.1 Technical & Economic Feasibility Assessment
**** 2.3.2 Bill of Materials & Tooling Selection
**** 2.3.3 PERT Chart & Milestone Scheduling

** 3. Core Codec Build <<phase>>
*** 3.1 Encoder Implementation
**** 3.1.1 Strided-Conv Downsampler (PyTorch)
**** 3.1.2 Shape Validation & Unit Tests
*** 3.2 Decoder Implementation & Integration
**** 3.2.1 Transposed-Conv Upsampler
**** 3.2.2 End-to-End Autoencoder Assembly (encode / decode / forward)
*** 3.3 Latent Quantization
**** 3.3.1 Uniform Scalar Affine Quantizer
**** 3.3.2 Global vs. Per-Channel Calibration
**** 3.3.3 Fixed Calibration from Training Split
*** 3.4 Entropy Coding
**** 3.4.1 Empirical Per-Channel Frequency Model
**** 3.4.2 Arithmetic (Range) Coder From First Principles
*** 3.5 .nvc Bitstream Format
**** 3.5.1 Header & Container Specification
**** 3.5.2 NVCWriter / NVCReader Implementation
**** 3.5.3 Encode / Decode CLI Scripts

** 4. Model Training & Tuning <<phase>>
*** 4.1 Training Loop Implementation
**** 4.1.1 Trainer (Train / Validate Epoch Loops)
**** 4.1.2 Checkpointing & Resume Logic
*** 4.2 Baseline Training Run
**** 4.2.1 CPU Smoke Test
**** 4.2.2 Full Baseline Training Pass
*** 4.3 Hyperparameter Tuning
**** 4.3.1 Learning Rate / Batch Size / Latent Channel Sweep
**** 4.3.2 Best Checkpoint Selection

** 5. Evaluation & Validation <<phase>>
*** 5.1 Reconstruction & Qualitative Validation
**** 5.1.1 Test-Split Reconstruction Script
**** 5.1.2 Visual Comparison Grids
*** 5.2 Quantitative Performance Evaluation
**** 5.2.1 MSE / PSNR Metrics
**** 5.2.2 BPP & Compression Ratio Benchmarking
**** 5.2.3 MS-SSIM & Codec Comparison (H.264 / H.265)
